## Summary

I want to be able to specify multiple inputs/outputs in the `"pre-build"` part of `moon.pkg.json`.

## Motivation

I was writing a MoonBit module to generate MoonBit code to be used in another module, and I used to have a code generator that generates two MoonBit source code files. However, this pre-build task cannot be properly modeled after the `"pre-build"` tasks in the `moon.pkg.json`. The `moon.pkg.json` I was using looks roughly like this:

```jsonc
{
  "pre-build": [
    {
      "input": "../../bin/generate/nn/tuple/main.mbt",
      "output": "nn_tuple.mbt",
      "command": "cd bin && moon run generate/nn/tuple && moon fmt"
    }
  ],
  // ...
}
```

The `"input"` part should be empty or some special value so that the command is run every time no matter what, and the `"output"` part should contains multiple `.mbt` files because the code generator used above will generate two MoonBit files.

## Detailed Description

My proposal is to support:

1. Empty input: the command will be executed every time to produce the outputs:

   ```json
   {
     "pre-build": [{
       "output": "a.mbt",
       "command": "command that generate a.mbt"
     }]
   }
   ```

2. Multiple inputs: the command will be executed when any of the input files have changed.

   ```json
   {
     "pre-build": [{
       "inputs": ["a.mbt", "b.mbt"],
       "output": "c.mbt"
       "command": "command that takes a.mbt and b.mbt and outputs c.mbt"
     }]
   }
   ```

3. Multiple outputs: the command will be executed when any of the output files are missing.

   ```json
   {
     "pre-build": [{
       "input": "a.mbt",
       "outputs": ["b.mbt", "c.mbt"]
       "command": "command that takes a.mbt and generates b.mbt and c.mbt"
     }]
   }
   ```

I thought supporting zero output would make sense somehow, but I can't think of any viable usage for it.

## Related Issues

I don't aware any of existing issue, pull requests, or discussions on this.

